#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:6
#: 0975ece0908c4461ad0e83f41fbba607
msgid "Synthetic Current Sensor/Analog Voltage Monitor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:8
#: d414f901031f4c899ff5fdb6924d03e3
msgid "Most autopilots have provisions for an external current sensor (normally as part of an external power module or ESC) or an integrated current sensor. For those using an external sensor, either using a power module or esc with current sensor or telemetry is not desirable due to weight or other considerations. In those cases, it may still be desired to obtain a measure of the current for either consumption reporting or other uses. This battery monitor backend provides a current estimate based on throttle position as well as the normal analog voltage reporting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:10
#: bfcc1a33e3f34f7eb5bf75d57fc7b921
msgid "currently this estimate is accurate only for Plane, Blimp, and Rover primary motors. Multicopter and QuadPlane VTOL mode current estimates are inaccurate and not recommended for use. Future improvements to provide accurate Multicopter and QuadPlane VTOL modes estimates are planned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:13
#: 5dad55b08eff45ce89e12b7637bae671
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:14
#: 14b1e2f22e0f4a5388d050561add459b
msgid "the following examples are for the first Battery Monitor. The parameter names will be ``BATTx`` prefaced for other monitors usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:16
#: 056a5027c926438db5c367a045b7a1e9
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR <BATT_MONITOR>` = 25"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:18
#: ce7d6f20c1e744a3ab4457a5a528b35d
msgid "For Voltage, the normal Analog Sensor parameters apply:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:20
#: 78e9765a8dd649ecb6b5a8f9c4df5277
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_PIN<BATT_VOLT_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` The autopilot pin connected to the power module's voltage pin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:21
#: 302eee8cc3794900a05b45c5d97acaf9
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_MULT<BATT_VOLT_MULT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` converts the analog voltage received from the power module's voltage pin to the battery's voltage. Provided on the :ref:`autopilot's hardware page:<common-autopilots>` or manufacturers page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:23
#: 129f8cb0b4b449579a344efe94de1b92
msgid "For the Current, some of the normal analog current sensor parameters have been re-tasked to save flash and their names are therefore a bit misleading in this application:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:25
#: 231f2d219ff54ba8b720e045759ce8bc
msgid ":ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` is the MAXIMUM current at full battery voltage in amps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:26
#: 4622a01f59d44016ac8a23ee87edb0db
msgid ":ref:`BATT_AMP_OFFSET <BATT_AMP_OFFSET__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` is the idle current (zero throttle) of the system in amps accounting for peripherals, video,etc. Normally in the 0.3 to 0.5 range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:27
#: dc0940d7c0dd4122b3a889c642980520
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MAX_VOLT<BATT_MAX_VOLT>` is the MAXIMUM fresh battery voltage. Used to scale the estimate as the battery voltage decreases during use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:29
#: 8b52616530234ae09cdc557edcf60fef
msgid "Calibration of the :ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` value can either be done on the bench with a current meter, or iteratively by estimating an initial value, operating for while, measuring the amount of current needed to restore the battery to full charge, and using that value and a flight log's or OSD's total consumed mah for the flight to adjust the parameter value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:31
#: 47131834a1b6446fb92f75d4889a8fb6
msgid "new value = old value * (mah returned to batt/log or OSD value of consumed mah)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-synthetic-current-monitor.rst:33
#: f5c63f81535f45aeb64dc8b5903ab26c
msgid "one or two iterations of the above may be required."
msgstr ""
